   "daf": "20b",
   "sentenceId": 15,
   "he": "דִּלְמָא לְמִכְתְּבִנְהוּ אֲזֻל? דִּכְתִיבִי בִּתְלָת יְדֵי סָפְרֵי.",
   "en": "The Gemara asks: «Perhaps» the three «went» to one scribe «to write» the promissory notes, and the notes were then lost together. The Gemara answers that the mishna is referring to a case «where» the promissory notes «are written in the handwriting of three» different «scribes.»"
  },
  {
   "id": "bava_metzia.20b.17",
   "daf": "20b",
   "sentenceId": 16,
   "he": "וְדִלְמָא לְקַיּוֹמִינְהוּ אֲזֻל? מַלְוֶה מְקַיֵּים שְׁטָרֵיהּ, לֹוֶה לָא מְקַיֵּים שְׁטָרֵיהּ.",
   "en": "The Gemara suggests: «And perhaps» the three debtors «went» to the court in order «to ratify» the promissory notes, and they lost them there. The Gemara answers: It is the «creditor» who «ratifies his» promissory «note;» the «debtor does not ratify his» promissory «note.»"
  }
 ],
